# Talk about a good deed (doc 56, topic deed). One of the two has heard of it and the other hasn't. {subject} is how the
# teller names the doer: a name they were given (known=yes), or how the doer looked (known=no: "a grey wolf with a torn
# ear"), so it sits mid-sentence. {deed} is what was done, as a phrase after "who" or "they" ("drove the bandits off the
# road at the ford"). Speak of the doer as "they". Alternatives are written in parallel.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- By name

scene dd_heard_named
when topic=deed topic.known=yes
a : Have you heard? #topic.subject# #topic.deed#. | Word is #topic.subject# #topic.deed#. | You know #topic.subject#? They #topic.deed#.
b : Did they now. | #topic.subject#? Good for them. | I hadn't heard that.
a : So they say. | It's all round the market. | I had it from someone who saw.

scene dd_named_doubt
when topic=deed topic.known=yes
a : They're saying #topic.subject# #topic.deed#. | #topic.subject# #topic.deed#, apparently. | Heard #topic.subject# #topic.deed#.
b[guard] : We heard something of it at the watch-house.
b[old] : In my day nobody did a thing like that for free.
b : I'll believe it when I hear it twice. | Is that so? | Well, well.
a : You'll hear it twice by supper. | It is. | It's true, I tell you.

scene dd_named_merchant
when topic=deed topic.known=yes here.place=market
a : #topic.subject# came through here, you know. They #topic.deed#. | Sold #topic.subject# bread last week. Turns out they #topic.deed#. | #topic.subject#, the one who #topic.deed#. I've served them.
b[merchant] : Then give them a good price next time.
b : Fancy that. | A good customer, then. | Small world.
a : I will. | The best kind. | Isn't it.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- By look

scene dd_heard_look
when topic=deed topic.known=no
a : Heard about the one who #topic.deed#? | Someone #topic.deed#, so they say. | Have you heard? Some wolf #topic.deed#.
b : Who was it? | No. Who? | Go on.
a : Nobody knows the name. #topic.subject#, they said. | #topic.subject#, by the sound of it. Never gave a name. | A stranger. #topic.subject#.
b : Keep an eye out, then. | I'd like to buy them a drink. | Funny, not leaving a name.

scene dd_look_watch
when topic=deed topic.known=no
a : Did you hear someone #topic.deed#? | Somebody #topic.deed#, I hear. | There's talk someone #topic.deed#.
b[child] : Was it a hero? Did they have a sword?
b[guard] : We'd like a word with them. A thank-you, I mean.
b : Who? | Never heard. | Who'd do that?
a : #topic.subject#, apparently. | They say #topic.subject#. | #topic.subject#, no name given.

scene dd_look_curious
when topic=deed topic.known=no here.place=tavern
a : They say #topic.subject# #topic.deed#. Came in here after, too. | #topic.subject# sat right there, the night after they #topic.deed#. | You remember #topic.subject#? They #topic.deed#.
b[innkeeper] : I poured them a drink. Never said a word about it.
b : Never! | Which one was that? | I'd not have guessed.
a : Quiet ones often are. | By the hearth. | Neither would I.
